    {
      "id": "curalink",
      "title": "CuraLink",
      "description": "An Integrated Approach to Revolutionizing Medication Management and Access",
      "tags": [
        "Healthcare infrastructure",
        "AI"
      ],
      "preview": "/assets/images/curalink-frame-1410125354.png",
      "lead": "An Integrated Approach to Revolutionizing Medication Management and Access",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "labels": [],
          "text": [],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/assets/images/O0eropNKyrn2PiddrqZfKc7UWYk.png",
              "original": "/assets/images/O0eropNKyrn2PiddrqZfKc7UWYk.png"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/assets/images/pqVSqJqQWGvhh9zKzQ4cAUJGOA4.png",
              "original": "/assets/images/pqVSqJqQWGvhh9zKzQ4cAUJGOA4.png"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/assets/images/uyKgfgq2ylgIXte7Grx5yITMY.png",
              "original": "/assets/images/uyKgfgq2ylgIXte7Grx5yITMY.png"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "labels": [
            "OVERVIEW"
          ],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "This case study showcases how I balanced technological solutions to address the fragmented medication management system, undertaken as a solo bootcamp project. Discover the strategic user research and design conceptualization behind CuraLink, an app designed to empower patients through real-time pharmacy data, AI-driven adherence support, and streamlined healthcare communication."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Designed and Developed with -"
            }
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/assets/images/XU8QoY1BOh8RTykKVMvgFZXr1g.jpg",
              "original": "/assets/images/XU8QoY1BOh8RTykKVMvgFZXr1g.jpg"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "labels": [
            "MY ROLE"
          ],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "As the solo designer for CuraLink, my role involved an 8-week research and a 4-week prototyping phase. My responsibilities encompassed user research, system design, prototyping, illustration, user flow creation, and storytelling. Utilizing Miro, Figma, and Photoshop, my responsibilities often blended with product ownership and business analysis, ensuring CuraLink's desirability, viability, and technical feasibility"
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [
            "PROBLEM"
          ],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "From Fragmented to Flowing"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Medication access and adherence is fragmented due to outdated tech and poor patient-pharmacy-provider connectivity."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Patients with chronic diseases don't take medications as prescribed, leading to poor health outcomes and high costs."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Americans provide unpaid care, many managing medications. 72% caregivers report feeling overwhelmed, especially when managing multiple prescriptions."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Prescriptions are abandoned at the pharmacy if the out-of-pocket cost is above $50. 29% Adults in the U.S. report not taking medicines as prescribed due to cost."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Medication errors happen during transitions in care, often due to to poor communication. Upto 70% of adverse drug events are preventable with better coordination."
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "What happens when care moves beyond the clinic?"
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [
            "RESEARCH"
          ],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Telehealth now accounts for ~40% of digital health, evolving into a core layer of care as the broader market moves toward a $1T future. Health management is no longer episodic, it happens in real time, integrated into everyday life."
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Digital health is projected to cross $1T by 2034"
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Healthcare today spans providers, pharmacies, devices, and caregivers, but these systems rarely work together. As a result, users are left to navigate complexity on their own, turning care into a fragmented and overwhelming experience."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "While technology is expanding access, it often fails to support how people actually live with their health. Especially for older adults, poorly designed systems create friction, reducing confidence, independence, and the overall sense of care."
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [],
          "text": [],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/assets/images/jDQYl7IPiCvIENdBIVSYoBJ86Cc.jpg",
              "original": "/assets/images/jDQYl7IPiCvIENdBIVSYoBJ86Cc.jpg"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/assets/images/6kNnMtGNMuOU3hu5DonqxDwYEnM.jpg",
              "original": "/assets/images/6kNnMtGNMuOU3hu5DonqxDwYEnM.jpg"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "labels": [],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "People can access care more easily, but navigating it is still confusing"
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [],
          "text": [],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/assets/images/uT5unIYvwf3HfKbSyVJ49hDfg4.jpg",
              "original": "/assets/images/uT5unIYvwf3HfKbSyVJ49hDfg4.jpg"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/assets/images/IH4sK4UPhmv1GVo2Je53fd2WK7o.jpg",
              "original": "/assets/images/IH4sK4UPhmv1GVo2Je53fd2WK7o.jpg"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "labels": [
            "FOUNDATIONS"
          ],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Empathetic design tailored for aging users"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Clear communication of personalized health insights"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Inclusive accessibility across devices, bandwidths, and literacy levels"
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [
            "KEY DRIVERS"
          ],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "1 in 6 people globally will be aged 60+ by 2030"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "40+ U.S. states have adopted telehealth coverage parity laws"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "AI -powered tools are reshaping adherence through predictive, personalized care"
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "How might we enhance medication access, communication, and adherence through a connected, user-centered experience?"
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [
            "QUALITATIVE INTERVIEWS"
          ],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Streamline medication management, strengthen patient-pharmacy-provider connectivity, and empower users with real time insights to improve adherence and access."
            }
          ],
          "media": []
        },
        {
          "labels": [],
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "David"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "55, Concerned Caregiver Son"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Manages meds for his mother (82) with Dementia, Arthritis, AFib (8 meds). Goal: Ensure mother's adherence, streamline coordination. Pain Point: Confirming intake, refill complexity, communication gaps"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Elena"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "48, Proactive Polypharmacy Manager"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Manages Type 2 Diabetes and Hypertension, High Cholesterol (6 meds). Goal: Simplify routine, avoid interactions, save money. Pain Point: Forgetting doses, tracking refills, cost surprises."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Margaret"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "76, Independent but Cautious Senior"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Manages Osteoarthritis, Hypertension, GERD (4 meds). Goal: Maintain independence, manage costs, ensure accuracy. Pain Point: Forgetfulness, cost worries, tech/privacy concerns."
            }
          ],
